-- The place tree takes in the official registers of origin: EU wine and
-- spirit GIs (eAmbrosia) with each country's own levels, US AVAs (TTB),
-- Australian, New Zealand, Chilean, Argentine, South African, Uruguayan,
-- Brazilian and Canadian GIs, Scotch whisky regions, Japanese sake GIs and
-- every Korean 시·도 and 시·군·구. A place that had been in the tree keeps its
-- key and gains the register's names as synonyms; one the register sets
-- inside a narrower place of the same branch moves there (포이악 under 오 메독).
-- Every Korean 구 is named with its city (서울 마포구). Keys stay, so no
-- bottle changes. The rows are the dictionary's projection, rendered from
-- catalog/dictionary/places.json.

